   "subject": "BUG Report: time data in Renjin",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Renjin community,<div><br></div><div>I am working with time series data in Renjin. I currently met this problem: (all codes in R)</div><div><br></div><div>Given 2 characters of date, for example:</div><div><b>t1 &lt;- &quot;Tue Feb 17 10:30:00 2015&quot;</b></div><div><b>t2 &lt;- &quot;Tue Feb 17 16:20:24 2015&quot;</b></div><div><br></div><div>And change the data type to date:</div><div><div><b>tt1 &lt;- strptime(t1, &quot;%a %b %d %H:%M:%S %Y&quot;)</b></div><div><b>tt2 &lt;- strptime(t2, &quot;%a %b %d %H:%M:%S %Y&quot;)</b></div></div><div><br></div><div>Calculate the time difference:</div><div><b>td &lt;- tt2 - tt1</b></div><div><br></div><div>If in GNU R, the result is &quot;<span style=\"font-size:10.4pt;line-height:1.2;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\">Time difference of 5.84 hours</font></span>&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>But in Renjin, the result is &quot;<font face=\"times new roman, serif\">Time difference of -10 mins</font>&quot;</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
